+# Initial reporting owner context recovery
+
+The optional initial branch of `tools/step5-reporting-owner-recovery.mjs` admits
+exactly impact-initial round1, unit **all**. It authenticates all three actual
+original reporting lanes and creates three new persistent native contexts. It
+never resumes an unavailable session or adopts its old review credit. Existing
+repeat recovery and default initial dispatch remain unchanged.
+
+Install only after root pauses/drains the actual5.2 controller and all writers,
+and after independent code review. Restart the controller after installing the
+reviewed code because cached ESM imports can survive edits. Preserve original
+reports, packs, prompts, native attempts/results and all counters/repair budgets.
+No mathematical source edit is part of admission; root owns recertification.
+
+Admission requires the actual paused/drained5.2 state and exact owner-gate
+request, all successful immutable Sol6.1/high original executions, null original
+session homes, exact assigned review inventories, unique bounded pending IDs,
+and at least one actual pending/uncertain obligation. Every lane's fresh floor
+is its entire original assignment plus all pending consumers. Floors must be
+disjoint; overlapping duties require separately designed sequential recovery,
+never concurrent writers or silently dropped ownership. Genuine reader identity
+conflicts fail closed. Original created_items and decisions must be empty.
+
+Ordinary original collection remains strict. The separate immutable historical
+scheduling observation has reviews:[], historical_reviews containing all exact
+original rows, native_acceptance:false, and the exact original uncertainty
+errors. No other malformed native report/error is deferred. Context matching
+cannot turn a historical uncertain row into current coverage. The first native
+advance rechecks actual current inputs; fresh uncertainty remains invalid.
+
+Root prepares existing mechanical preparation/inputs files with ok:true,
+metadata_checked:true, native_execution_coverage:false,
+mathematical_review_claimed:false and the exact full manifest-selected source
+vector (raw/guard hashes) and manifest guards. The recorder computes actual
+review contexts and authenticates current sources and transitive supplier
+contexts before first scheduling.
+
+The unavailable evidence file is `{run,rows:[...]}` with exactly lanes1/2/3.
+Each row contains run, phase:'impact-initial', round:1, unit, actual session_id,
+session_home:null, original_report_sha256, original_result_sha256,
+original_context_unavailable:true, journal_payloads_read:false,
+matching_session_paths:[], confirmed_by:'/root', confirmed_at, a substantive
+reason and observation:{path,sha256}. Each separate read-only observation must
+identify run/session_id and journal_payloads_read:false, matching_session_paths:[]
+for that actual session. Bind genuine captured native report/result bytes; do
+not read credentials or archive journal payloads.
+
+At the actual hold, root calls:
+
+```js
+await previewReportingOwnerRecovery(root, run, 'impact-initial', 1, 'all', payload);
+await recordReportingOwnerRecovery(root, run, 'impact-initial', 1, 'all', payload);
+```
+
+The payload has exactly reason, preparation_file, preparation_inputs_file,
+session_unavailable_evidence_file. Use identical files/arguments after inspecting
+the read-only preview. For the machine-learning escalation the expected floors
+are71/72/80 (223 distinct subjects). Preview writes nothing. Recording archives
+actual state/request/current preparation and a separate historical scheduling
+observation. The immutable receipt path is
